<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johan Rudolf Thorbecke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798–1872</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Thorbecke</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johan Rudolf Thorbecke was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> liberal statesman and professor of law. He led the drafting of the constitutional revision of 1848, which introduced ministerial responsibility, direct elections to the Second Chamber and basic civil freedoms, establishing parliamentary government in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. He served three times as head of government, in 1849–1853, 1862–1866 and 1871–1872.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johan-rudolf-thorbecke.jpg" alt="Johan Rudolf Thorbecke" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johan Heinrich Neuman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johan_Heinrich_Neuman_-_Johan_Rudolf_Thorbecke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
